e in: v4.6.1-stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta (a0375dde9) - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8180) - AMD Ryzen 7 7800X3D 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 63.11 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen closing the project a new project after removing a breakpoint in a script I get this message with the number of leaked RIDs increasing for each time I removed a breakpoint (with `--verbose`):\n> ERROR: 4 RID allocations of type 'PN18TextServerAdvanced22ShapedTextDataAdvancedE' were leaked at exit.\nWARNING: 4 ObjectDB instances were leaked at exit (run with `--verbose` for details).\n   at: cleanup (./core/object/object.cpp:2535)\nLeaked instance: TextParagraph:9223373756066504266 - Reference count: 1\nLeaked instance: TreeItem:1719194951244\nLeaked instance: TextParagraph:9223373756032949839 - Reference count: 1\nLeaked instance: TreeItem:1719161396817\nHint: Leaked instances typically happen when nodes are removed from the scene tree (with `remove_child()`) but not freed (with `free()` or `queue_free()`).\nOrphan StringName: line (static: 0, total: 1)\nOrphan StringName: metadata/line (static: 0, total: 1)\nOrphan StringName: Node (static: 3, total: 4)\nStringName: 3 unclaimed string names at exit.\n\nI think this function is relevant https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a0375dde960ee9dba46d461e0145123609691950/editor/debugger/script_editor_debugger.cpp#L1730\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create new project\n2. Open it through a terminal\n3. Create a scene with a node (I used Node2D) and add the default script\n4. Add a breakpoint and remove it again (also works with `Remove All Breakpoints`)\n5. Close the project\n6. The error message should appear in the terminal\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"h